- If curClippedDemand = 0:
    leadPump := 0;
    lagPump := 0;
    // Also maybe we want to reset prevLeadPump, prevLagPump? Not needed but we could. For next positive demand, we treat as initial selection. So we can set a flag bLeadSelected := FALSE; but we can infer from leadPump = 0. So we need to treat leadPump = 0 as "no lead pump selected yet". That works.

- If curClippedDemand > 0:

